# Remaining Zstd security controls

Qualify missing security behavior of the already reviewed upstream zstd 0.14.3 /
zstd-safe 8.2.0 candidate. This is not another compression/MTU algorithm or a
performance cohort. Root lock, deny policy, Rust 1.88 and qualification identity
remain exact. Existing M/S declines, original wide/239-case/oversize contracts
and first failures are not replaced. No adoption, publication, service, clock,
server, supervisor or product workload is involved.

Freeze the current root and the existing primary source archives before tests.
Review RUSTSEC-2026-0391/0398/0403 at the observed advisory DB revision. Do not run
known unsafe seekable/legacy old APIs merely to manufacture a native baseline.
Their source evidence and earlier context refusal remain; the candidate gets
explicit positive fault assertions. No paired old/new exploit or leak is claimed.

Two disjoint fixtures: (1) eight owned public-API controls; (2) exact upstream
zstd-safe library tests, with std + seekable and its original default features.
The latter is a selected-feature library gate, not all upstream integrations or
all optional features. Probe all-target/all-feature check/strict Clippy cannot
enable arbitrary dependency features; do not claim bindgen/cmake/Rust allocator
coverage. Keep those optional feature branches unqualified.

Public controls cover abandoned encoder/decoder jobs, both seekable readers with
end/past-end/u64::MAX offsets and zero/small capacities, failed legacy call
positions and reset, write/flush/normal drop/auto-flush/on-flush, all split points
of the exact six-byte upstream corrupt v0.7 frame, and valid modern roundtrips.
Source and exact diagnostic rows, not timing or heap samples, define the gate.
Bind actual compiler artifacts, complete native test listings, unchanged source/
lock/registry/HEAD and successful owned retirement. No filtering or ignored cases
may be hidden in totals. Confirm identical selected-feature catalogs on Windows
and GNU Rust 1.94 / 1.88 where cfg permits; report differences explicitly.

Original local review envelope: 1200 seconds, physical/native floor 4 GiB,
capacity polling/cleanup 5 seconds. GNU sessions keep 1100 seconds inside the
Windows owner. Streams precede preflight; output roots are exclusive and first
refusals remain. All production live checks and 300/60/10, test 5/10/45,
package/workspace 780/4800 contracts remain unchanged.

Security controls alone cannot accept S, erase MTU underestimation or establish
allocation/CPU/RSS/retained-memory non-regression. A distributable compatible
Chitchat package, real product/GNU/package/workspace gates and original execution/
recovery remain separate prerequisites.
